John Yamokoski wrote:
> Greetings,
> 
> I have the same freezing problem after compiling/installing/running an
> adeos patched kernel on an Ubuntu system. Unfortunately to uninstall
> gnome-power-manager I must also uninstall 'ubuntu-desktop'.. which I
> am not sure I want to do.
> 
> Any ideas? Do I need to switch to a different window manager? Is there
> some setting with gnome-power-manager I can set that will avoid the
> freezing?
> 
> I will also query the ubuntu community. If I hear anything back I will
> post it here.

Ok people. Please all stop thinking that you have the same problem as
Benoit. There are many ways to get freezes, it could be configuration
problems, irq sharing problems, adeos patch problems, drivers problems,
problems in real-time applications (such as infinite loop in a real-time
thread). So, stop jumping quickly to conclusions, do what we are asking
you, and provide feedback on your experiences.

